From 6a492a2e5da6d0dd74821176f8c8e17e445913af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaoyuping <yaoyuping@hygon.cn>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:16:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/24] eplb: fix Step5 EPLB (MoE block unwrap, mixed-dtype
 layers, skip metric); add touched-load and dump options

- _propagate_shared_tensors: unwrap .experts for MoE blocks (Step5) so
  layer eplb_state is found.
- rearrange_expert_weights_inplace: per-(shape, dtype) buffers; Step5's
  bf16 last MoE layers mismatched the fp8 buffer and hung the P2P transfer.
- ROCm skip check: imbalance = sum of per-layer max / sum of per-layer
  mean (layers sync at the combine), log the rearrange imbalance.
- VLLM_EPLB_TOUCHED_LOAD=1 records touched experts instead of tokens
  (token load is dominated by prefill); VLLM_EPLB_DUMP_PATH saves the
  placement.

On Step5 bs32 64k/4k neither online EPLB nor a statically applied
placement improved decode (1084 vs 1088 tok/s): MTP3 decode touches
nearly all experts on every rank.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 distributed/eplb/eplb_state.py        | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 distributed/eplb/rebalance_execute.py | 18 ++++++++--
 2 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/distributed/eplb/eplb_state.py b/distributed/eplb/eplb_state.py
